      "text": "\\newcommand{\\unreg}[1]{\\textcolor{orange!80!black}{#1}}   % computed, not yet registered"
    },
    {
      "line": 93,
      "text": "shotgun sequenced 551 soil samples to a median depth of 21.58~Gbp per sample (Fig.~\\ref{fig:design}a,b)."
    },
    {
      "line": 98,
      "text": "(Fig.~\\ref{fig:design}c). Full MIMAG assessment classified 126 as high quality and 5{,}312 as medium quality. Taxonomy throughout is GTDB release 232."
    },
    {
      "line": 108,
      "text": "GTDB label (Table~\\ref{tab:naming}). The latter is a proxy for reference naming coverage."
    },
    {
      "line": 111,
      "text": "\\caption{Mutually exclusive taxonomy depths among 5,438 representatives. The domain count is zero for both rules.}\\label{tab:naming}"
    },
    {
      "line": 153,
      "text": "alignment and estimation steps (Fig.~\\ref{fig:dark}a). The pooled distributions differ, and the groups also differ in sequence divergence: median"
    },
    {
      "line": 162,
      "text": "(Fig.~\\ref{fig:dark}c). These conditional intervals treat families as independent."
    },
    {
      "line": 179,
      "text": "median 0.427 and 97.0\\% below one (Fig.~\\ref{fig:dark}b). Both arms were evaluable for 9{,}029 families, and the shifted"
    },
    {
      "line": 211,
      "text": "calls (96.1\\%). The union of reciprocal-protein and DNA support covered 752/1{,}341 eligible dark calls (56.1\\%) and 70{,}354/81{,}533 annotated calls (86.3\\%). This union includes protein-supported calls that failed the nucleotide threshold; it is not a DNA-only detection rate. Protein sharing therefore understates the combined evidence for shared sequence in both groups (Fig.~\\ref{fig:dark}d--f). Across pairs, recovery of protein-shared calls ranged from 67.9\\% to 99.6\\%. In the post hoc subset of 20 pairs with at least 90\\% recovery, DNA support for protein-unshared calls was 496/940 (52.8\\%) for dark calls and 4{,}254/11{,}240 (37.8\\%) for annotated calls."
    },
    {
      "line": 232,
      "text": "cluster has no UniRef50 homolog; across the 5{,}438 representatives its median is 6.3\\% (Fig.~\\ref{fig:lineage}a)"
    },
    {
      "line": 239,
      "text": "(Fig.~\\ref{fig:lineage}b), and within Actinomycetota, Pseudomonadota and Bacteroidota genomes with a"
    },
    {
      "line": 267,
      "text": "237 pairs (Fig.~\\ref{fig:lineage}c). The contrast persists after this quality and abundance matching. In a separate comparison"
    },
    {
      "line": 322,
      "text": "TM-score of 0.5, compared with 101 of 3{,}013 controls (3.35\\%; Fig.~\\ref{fig:structural}a)."
    },
    {
      "line": 341,
      "text": "and 118 controls (Fig.~\\ref{fig:structural}b,c). Domain arrangement, extensions and uncertain"
    },
    {
      "line": 363,
      "text": "orthologues is 0.839 (median weighted nearest-taxon index 0.159; Fig.~\\ref{fig:reference}a)."
    },
    {
      "line": 372,
      "text": "the control (435) (Fig.~\\ref{fig:reference}b). Absence here is defined by the catalogue and the"
    },
    {
      "line": 379,
      "text": "by about one point (Fig.~\\ref{fig:reference}b). The larger-release sensitivity search recovered a small additional fraction. Against the complete"
    },
    {
      "line": 385,
      "text": "the medians range from 44 versus 50 locations in the shortest stratum to the values shown in Fig.~\\ref{fig:reference}c. The combined desert catalogue and SPIRE recover more dark families than the analytical MGnify90"
    },
